---
title: Normal Scale-Up Flow (High Queue Depth Detected)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant CA as Cluster Aggregator
    participant EI as Event Ingestion
    participant SC as Scheduler Core
    participant WS as World State
    participant SE as Scaling Engine
    participant PE as Placement Engine
    participant PX as Plan Executor
    participant CC as Cluster Client<br/>(us-west-1)
    participant VOL as Volcano<br/>(in-cluster)

    CA->>EI: vLLMMetrics(app=X, queue=12, kv_cache=0.85)
    EI->>SC: TriggerEvaluation

    SC->>WS: snapshot()
    WS-->>SC: WorldState snapshot

    SC->>SE: compute_target(app=X, vllm_metrics, profile)

    Note over SE: queue_depth=12 > HIGH_WATERMARK(10)<br/>kv_cache=0.85 = HIGH_WATERMARK<br/>Both signals indicate scale-up needed

    SE-->>SC: target=5 (was 3, need +2)

    SC->>PE: compute_placement(snapshot, targets)

    Note over PE: Find best clusters for 2 new replicas<br/>Score by: cache tier (dominant), fragmentation, balance

    PE-->>SC: PlacementDecisions:<br/>scale_ups=[<br/>  (X, us-west-1, prefer=[node-3], cache=LOCAL_NVME),<br/>  (X, eu-central-1, prefer=[node-2], cache=GPU_MEMORY)<br/>]

    SC->>PX: execute(plan)

    par Execute in parallel per cluster
        PX->>CC: create_pod(X, constraints)
        CC->>VOL: Pod spec with nodeAffinity

        Note over VOL: Evaluate preferred nodes<br/>Check GPU availability<br/>Bin-pack decision

        VOL->>VOL: bind(node-3)
        VOL-->>CC: Pod scheduled on node-3

        CC->>CC: wait_for_running(timeout)
        CC-->>PX: Pod running
    end

    PX-->>SC: ExecutionResult: success

    Note over SC: Update internal state<br/>Log metrics
